{"status":"completed","summary":"Inventory web applications are running persistently on node2 and node3 at port 8080. node1 runs nginx on port 80 and round-robins requests across both backends. All three nodes were restarted sequentially and fully recovered with changed boot IDs.","actions_performed":["Created and enabled the inventory systemd service on node2 and node3.","Opened TCP/8080 persistently on both backend firewalls.","Installed and enabled nginx on node1.","Configured a shared round-robin upstream for node2:8080 and node3:8080.","Enabled persistent HTTP firewall and SELinux proxy access on node1.","Verified API, HTML content, and alternating backend responses.","Restarted node1, node2, and node3 individually and verified recovery after each restart."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Inventory application on node2:8080","command_ids":["cmd-c0944bac230b49e3","cmd-17ba1f86656649e8"],"summary":"Port 8080 is listening; the enabled service returns node2 health and inventory data, including after restart."},{"requirement":"Inventory application on node3:8080","command_ids":["cmd-b631077bc8d24b7d","cmd-9ec3cd61cd9146b3"],"summary":"Port 8080 is listening; the enabled service returns node3 health and inventory data, including after restart."},{"requirement":"node1 load-balances incoming HTTP requests on port 80","command_ids":["cmd-94e88ca384384841","cmd-28748302ed6b478e","cmd-92f27d87fca647fc","cmd-b3d87c4d3fb74c8d"],"summary":"nginx is enabled and listening on port 80; configuration validates; requests alternate between node2 and node3; a remote request from node2 receives HTTP 200 through node1."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-c3314b0d6b804147","cmd-9b2440d9c94d45c5","cmd-198d216370524a28"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID df8bab0d…; reboot acknowledged; new boot ID ecb02dbc… with nginx, inventory data, and both backends recovered."},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8bdcc5e